<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Free State of Coburg</h1><p class="st-meta">1918 CE – 1920 CE · capital Coburg</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Brief Franconian republic that, after a 1919 referendum, chose to join Bavaria rather than Thuringia.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-edward-duke-of-saxe-coburg-and-gotha">Charles Edward of Saxe-Coburg and Gotha</a> abdicated in November 1918. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coburg">Coburg</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gotha">Gotha</a>, legally separate since 1826, went their own ways: Gotha joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringia">Thuringia</a>, while Coburg became a free state of its own, with its parliament meeting in Coburg.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The free state existed only briefly and had few powers beyond managing the transition. Its main question was its future: too small to survive alone, it had to choose between the new Thuringian state and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>. In a referendum on 30 November 1919, about 88 per cent of voters chose Bavaria, partly because of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coburg">Coburg's</a> Franconian ties and Bavaria's favourable terms.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Under a state treaty <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coburg">Coburg</a> joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-state-of-bavaria">Free State of Bavaria</a> on 1 July 1920, keeping certain guarantees for its institutions.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/free-state-of-coburg.jpg" alt="Free State of Coburg" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: David Liuzzo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flagge_Herzogtum_Sachsen-Coburg-Gotha_(1911-1920).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1918 CE – 1920 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Coburg</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German, East Franconian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Freistaat Coburg</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1919&amp;focus=free-state-of-coburg" aria-label="Free State of Coburg on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4931 431 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Free State of Coburg lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5251 687L5251 687M5251 687L5269 749"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5251 687h0M5269 749h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5251 687h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5251 687h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Coburg. <a href="/atlas?year=1919&amp;focus=free-state-of-coburg">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
